  "text": " difficulté: 8 out of 10\n ============================================================================================================\n\n1.  Identify which arcs are closest to each other.\n\n 처음에 우리는 (2+15, 13)에서 서로 가까운 세 개의 원을 발견했습니다. 이러한 원의 한 사람이 선의 가장자리가 된다는 것은, 우리의 첫번째 적용이 촉진됩니다.\n\n2.  Determine the lengths of the arcs whose endpoints lie on the shortest side.\n\n Ιhe shortest side of the hexagon consists of two arcs. In fact, one of the arcs between areas 15 and 21 in radiation 枋라는 세 개의 원 중 두 개가 서로 연결되는 25봤습니다. 이제, 어떤 두원이 arcs의 주사위也是 십니다, 왜냐하면 우리는 2이 2에서 나가는진 실제로 1일차의 \"*\"것입니다.\n\n3.  Find the area enclosed by the hexagon.\n\n Ιhe area enclosed by the hexagon can be found by dividing it into six smaller shapes each of which is a sector of a circle. The total area of the triangle is equal to the sum of each sector's area. We sum up the sectors' area plus that of the triangle, forming the closed shape of the hexagon.\n\n### Solution:\n\n1. **Identify which arcs are closest to each other:**\n   - We have three circles with radii 7, 13, and 15 units.\n   - The shortest side of the hexagon is 25 units, which consists of two arcs.\n   - The arcs between the circles with radii 13 and 15 sum up to 25 units.\n\n2. **Determine the lengths of the arcs whose endpoints lie on the shortest side:**\n   - The arc between circles with radii 13 and 15 is 25 units.\n   - The arc between circles with radii 15 and 7 is 25 units.\n   - The arc between circles with radii 7 and 13 must be the remaining part of the hexagon.\n\n3. **Find the area enclosed by the hexagon:**\n   - The hexagon is composed of six sectors of circles.\n   - The area of each sector can be calculated using the formula \\( \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} r^2 \\theta \\), where \\( r \\) is the radius and \\( \\theta \\) is the central angle in radians.\n   - The sum of the sectors' areas plus the area of the triangle formed by the radii gives the total area of the hexagon.\n\nLet's calculate the area step-by-step:\n\n1. **Calculate the area of the triangle:**\n   - The triangle is formed by the radii connecting the points of intersection of the arcs.\n   - The area of the triangle can be calculated using the formula for the area of a triangle with sides \\( a, b, \\) and \\( c \\) and angle \\( A \\) opposite side \\( a \\):\n     \\[\n     \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} ab \\sin(C)\n     \\]\n   - Here, \\( a = 13 \\), \\( b = 15 \\), and \\( C = \\pi \\) (since the points are on the same circle).\n     \\[\n     \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 13 \\times 15 \\times \\sin(\\pi) = 0\n     \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the area of the sectors:**\n   - The area of each sector is given by \\( \\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} r^2 \\theta \\), where \\( \\theta \\) is the central angle in radians.\n   - For the sectors with radius 13 and 15, \\( \\theta = \\frac{25}{13} \\) and \\( \\theta = \\frac{25}{15} \\), respectively.\n     \\[\n     \\text{Area of sector with radius 13} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 13^2 \\times \\frac{25}{13} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 13 \\times 25 = \\frac{212.5}{2} = 106.25\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     \\text{Area of sector with radius 15} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 15^2 \\times \\frac{25}{15} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 15 \\times 25 = \\frac{375}{2} = 187.5\n     \\]\n\n3. **Total area of the hexagon:**\n   - The total area is the sum of the areas of the six sectors plus the area of the triangle.\n     \\[\n     \\text{Total area} = 106.25 + 187.5 + 106.25 + 187.5 + 106.25 + 187.5 + 0 = 882.5\n     \\]\n\nThe final answer is \\( \\boxed{882.5} \\).",
